# Puca: nightly DB backup + 5-min health check  ->  /etc/cron.d/puca
#
# These paths must match where you installed the scripts. They assume a fresh
# install (/opt/puca). If your deployment lives somewhere else, edit both lines
# — cron cannot detect it, though the scripts themselves resolve their OWN names
# and will abort loudly (exit 78, which cron mails to you) rather than quietly
# back up or monitor nothing. See names.sh.
#
# names.sh must sit beside them: the scripts source it from their own directory.
0 3 * * * root /opt/puca/backup.sh
*/5 * * * * root /opt/puca/healthcheck.sh
